The integral over $[k, k+1]$ is $e^k I$ (with $k=0$). Summing gives geometric series. $J/I = \frac{e^N-1}{e-1}$. The ratio is an integer only when $e^N-1$ is an integer multiple of $e-1$. The only integer $N \ge 1$ satisfying this is $N=1$ (ratio=1).

